  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/4BBD48">Definition <span data-tag="4BBD48">5.3.3.1</span>.</a>$\kappa $-closed Let $\kappa $ be a regular cardinal. We will say that an $\infty $-category $\calC $ is <em>$\kappa $-closed</em> if every diagram $p: K \rightarrow \calC $ indexed by a $\kappa $-small simplicial set $K$ admits a colimit $\overline{p}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC $. </p>
